  "step_3": "The decision reason is based on minimizing variance, which favors Lottery B (lower variance). However, the individual's justification centers on expected value (higher for A) and the ratio of probability to prize, concluding that Lottery A is better despite its higher variance. The individual does not consider or mention variance at any point. The information considered (expected value, probability difference, prize magnitude) is different from that relevant to the variance-based reason. The decision rule (preferring lower variance) is also inconsistent with the justification (preferring higher expected value and better probability-to-prize ratio). Therefore, the individual did not use the variance-based reason to make the decision. The assessment is certain that the reason was not used.",
